<!--
    LittleGPTracker input mapping for RK3566 / ROCKNIX handhelds.

    Verified on a Powkiddy RGB30, whose pad is presented by the kernel as
    "retrogame_joypad" (rocknix-singleadc-joypad).  It is the same pad, with
    the same button numbering, on the other RK3566 handhelds ROCKNIX supports,
    so these indices should hold for the Anbernic RG-ARC and friends too.

    Button numbers are raw SDL joystick indices.  SDL numbers the buttons of
    this pad in ascending evdev key code order, which works out as:

        0  BTN_SOUTH  face button at the bottom   (labelled B on an RGB30)
        1  BTN_EAST   face button on the right    (labelled A on an RGB30)
        2  BTN_NORTH  face button on the top      (labelled Y)
        3  BTN_WEST   face button on the left     (labelled X)
        4  BTN_TL     L1            5  BTN_TR     R1
        6  BTN_TL2    L2            7  BTN_TR2    R2
        8  BTN_SELECT              9  BTN_START
       10  BTN_MODE  (guide)      11  BTN_THUMBL   L3
       12  BTN_THUMBR R3
       13  BTN_DPAD_UP           14  BTN_DPAD_DOWN
       15  BTN_DPAD_LEFT         16  BTN_DPAD_RIGHT

    This matches EmulationStation's own es_input.cfg for "retrogame_joypad",
    which is the authoritative description of how this hardware is wired.

    The D-pad arrives as four ordinary buttons rather than a hat, so it is
    mapped with "but:" and not "hat:".

    To re-derive the numbers on a different device, set DUMPEVENT to YES in
    config.xml, press a button and read the "but(0):N" line in log.txt.
-->
<MAPPINGS>

    <!-- D-pad -->
    <MAP src="but:0:13" dst="/event/up" />
    <MAP src="but:0:14" dst="/event/down" />
    <MAP src="but:0:15" dst="/event/left" />
    <MAP src="but:0:16" dst="/event/right" />

    <!-- Face buttons.  The RGB30 labels the right hand button A and the
         bottom button B, which is the opposite way round from the evdev
         BTN_SOUTH/BTN_EAST naming. -->
    <MAP src="but:0:1" dst="/event/a" />
    <MAP src="but:0:0" dst="/event/b" />

    <!-- Shoulders -->
    <MAP src="but:0:4" dst="/event/lshoulder" />
    <MAP src="but:0:5" dst="/event/rshoulder" />

    <!-- Start -->
    <MAP src="but:0:9" dst="/event/start" />

    <!-- The left analog stick doubles as the D-pad: on a 720x720 handheld the
         stick is often more comfortable for scrolling long patterns.  Remove
         these four lines if stick drift ever causes phantom key presses. -->
    <MAP src="joy:0:0-" dst="/event/left" />
    <MAP src="joy:0:0+" dst="/event/right" />
    <MAP src="joy:0:1-" dst="/event/up" />
    <MAP src="joy:0:1+" dst="/event/down" />

</MAPPINGS>
